# Everything on x-profile-location.pages.dev moved to x-pat.pages.dev.
#
# `:splat` carries the rest of the path through, so /x-about-this-account lands
# on the same page rather than the homepage — which is what preserves the
# ranking of the individual pages rather than just the root.
#
# Query strings are forwarded automatically; fragments are never sent to the
# server, so they survive by virtue of the browser reapplying them.
#
# 301 (permanent) is deliberate: it is what tells Google to transfer the old
# URLs' signals to the new ones. It is also cached hard by browsers, so this
# line is effectively irreversible for anyone who has hit it once — do not
# deploy it until x-pat.pages.dev actually serves the site.
/*  https://x-pat.pages.dev/:splat  301
